Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `name` was consumed by `name.move()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/E0121_lambda_move_outer_use.jet:5:11
    |
  5 |     print(name)
    |           ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/E0121_lambda_move_outer_use.jet:3:25
    |
  3 |     f: fn() -> String { name.move() }
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^ `name` moved to `name.move()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `name` after the move, or give `name.move()` a copy with `name.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
